# F1 FlashPoint – Implementation Plan

This document outlines the end-to-end software engineering plan for building the F1 FlashPoint app. It includes over 50 detailed implementation steps covering architecture, API design, dashboard integration, hosting, security, testing, and long-term maintenance. All steps follow principles of modularity, simplicity, and alignment with the core documents (PRD, App Flow, Tech Stack, Cursor Rules).

---

## 1. 📦 Project Setup & Scaffolding
1.1 Create monorepo with `backend/`, `scripts/`, `media/`, `dashboard/`, `tests/`
1.2 Initialize Git and link to GitHub repo
1.3 Set up `pyproject.toml` using Poetry (preferred) or `requirements.txt`
1.4 Configure pre-commit hooks (black, isort, flake8)
1.5 Set up `.env` structure and secrets template

---

## 2. 🧠 Core Backend Architecture
2.1 Create FastAPI server entrypoint in `main.py`
2.2 Structure app modules: `fetcher`, `insight_engine`, `composer`, `media_gen`, `poster`, `scheduler`, `admin_ui`
2.3 Add FastAPI routers for each module
2.4 Set up Jinja2 templating for dashboard
2.5 Add global config manager using Pydantic

---

## 3. 🔍 FastF1 Data Fetcher
3.1 Integrate FastF1 API and retrieve session metadata
3.2 Implement lap-by-lap and telemetry fetch
3.3 Normalize and cache output as JSON in `/data/`
3.4 Add dynamic race detection (last event + last updated)

---

## 4. 🧠 Insight Engine (Analyst)
4.1 Write comparator functions for historical vs. recent data
4.2 Extract storyline-worthy anomalies, rivalries, drama
4.3 Output tagged insight JSON bundle per race
4.4 Implement emotional tagging heuristics

